-- title:
--   Fibre model with cusp chart for X₀(N) at ℓ∤ N
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$ (so `NeZero N`), let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\nmid N$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime ℓ`, i.e. the image of $\ell$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in the nonunits of $A$, and assume the residue field of $A$ has characteristic $\ell$. The assertion is that there exists a term of the structure `FibreModel N A ℓ (ResidueField ↥A) (IsLocalRing.residue ↥A)` whose associated `CuspChart` property holds. Such a fibre model consists of two subrings $B_{\mathrm{fin}}, B_\infty$ of `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (modularFunctionFieldFull N)` (the field of Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the level-$N$ modular function field over $\mathbb Q$), each containing the image of $A$ under `constantsHom`, with $\bar\jmath$ and $\bar\jmath_N$ in $B_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $\bar\jmath^{-1}$ in $B_\infty$, each element of $B_{\mathrm{fin}}$ (resp. $B_\infty$) integral over the subring generated by the constants together with $\bar\jmath$ (resp. $\bar\jmath^{-1}$), together with ring homomorphisms $\pi_{\mathrm{fin}}, \pi_\infty$ to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField ↥A) N`, the subfield of Laurent series over the residue field generated by `jqModC` and `jqNModC`, acting on constants through the residue map, sending $\bar\jmath\mapsto$ `jqModC`, $\bar\jmath_N\mapsto$ `jqNModC`, $\bar\jmath^{-1}\mapsto$ `jqModC`$^{-1}$, and satisfying the remaining compatibilities recorded in `FibreModel`. The `CuspChart` condition adds that $\bar\jmath_N\cdot(\bar\jmath^{-1})^N\in B_\infty$ and that $\pi_\infty$ carries this element to `jqNModC`$\cdot$`jqModC`$^{-N}$.
--
--   This is the existence half of Igusa's good-reduction theorem for $X_0(N)$ at a prime $\ell$ not dividing the level, packaged as integral models of the $j$-finite and $j$-infinite charts of the modular function field together with a chart adapted to the cusps. It is the input to the constructions of place specialisations attached to a fibre model and to the resulting statements about residue fields of prolongation tuples.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_CharPModel_exists_fibreModel_cuspChart_of_not_dvd.lean

